# General rear sky layer: atmospheric flow v01

The v03 Skybox Blend remains a general texture layer suitable for atmospheric
veils and later Milky Way imagery. Existing rear dome UV2 and the foreground
cloud packing are preserved. UV V=0 is the zenith; V=1 is the horizon.

## Assets

New textures live under
`/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/PaintedCloud/v03/Evolution/SkyboxBlend/AtmosphereFlow_v01`.

- `T_AtmosphereVeil_v01`: linear RGB illumination, A continuous coverage.
- `T_AtmosphereFlow_v01`: linear RG signed flow encoded around 0.5, B local phase.
- Base output is 4096x2048, resampled from the supplied generated source, not
  native 4K painted detail. Flow data is 1024x512. Both wrap U and clamp V.

The current `MF_ImportedSkyFlow` now uses two offset samples with complementary
triangle weights; inactive samples reset invisibly. It no longer uses the flow
texture as a noise texture. Base alpha follows the identical warped UVs.

## BP controls

| Control | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| Skybox Source Color Blend | 0: atmospheric shading; 1: original RGB with tint/intensity |
| Skybox Use Texture Alpha | 1: RGBA coverage; 0: luminance coverage for RGB sources |
| Skybox Flow Strength | Distortion amplitude; 0 disables distortion |
| Skybox Flow Speed | Cycles per second; 0 freezes the flow |
| Skybox Density | Continuous layer opacity |
| Skybox Contrast | Coverage exponent; lower values reveal faint veils |
| Skybox Atmosphere Blend | Move atmospheric cloud illumination toward the sky |
| Skybox Night Visibility | Minimum cloud illumination above the nighttime sky |
| Skybox Day Visibility | 0 hides the layer during daylight, useful for Milky Way |

Existing Base/Flow Texture, Tint, Intensity, Alpha Blend, Shadow Sky Blend,
rotation speed and layer blend remain editable. Null texture overrides use the
new defaults. For a future Milky Way texture, start with Source Color Blend=1,
Flow Strength=0, Day Visibility=0; choose alpha or luminance coverage according
to that texture. A Milky Way source itself is not included in this revision.

Cloud normal and FuzzyShading nodes/controls were removed from the active
combined sky material and v03 BP. Old normal textures remain as source backups.
The sky, foreground backdrop and shared night contrast use consistent rear
layer composition. Native Engine material and Blueprint APIs only.

Live checks: material/BP compile with zero errors; BP also zero warnings;
control min/max propagation and null-texture fallback; no direct MCP asset
dependencies; day/night viewport review. User time restored to 15.168001.
Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/PaintedEvolutionV03/AtmosphereRebuild/`.
